2026-08-25T00:01:31Z (RFD66606-1125) 'it. An argument is not, because a controlled vocabulary flattens an argument into a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1125  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:32Z (RFD66606-1125) 'specification. An essay also fails in a way ASD-STE100 never describes, since it can read as
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1125  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:33Z (RFD66606-1125) 'though a model wrote it. Neither kind owns a whole file either: a `DETAILS.md` carries a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1125  1 LINE
